  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- **Resetting a test database clears the pools of their own that Compze keeps on it, such as the type-id interner's, with the pool of the database's connection string; nothing public changes.**\n- **A test database's connection string limits its pool to ten connections, as the test databases of PostgreSQL and MySQL do,** rather than SqlClient's default of a hundred. A test that uses more connections at once waits for one, as it does on the other two, so a test that exhausts the pool, or deadlocks it, does so on SQL Server too.\n- **Requires newer minor versions of other Compze packages:** Compze.Sql.MicrosoftSql 0.8.0-alpha (was 0.5.0-alpha). Upgrading to this version upgrades each package listed here too, so their changelogs apply to this upgrade as well.",
